Now, where to put in test_smAgent.js — at the end probably. Let me check the end of the file and how suites are structured at the end.

For the smAgent tests I need a helper to extract the published snapshot JSON from the PUT command. The PUT command contains `-f content="$(printf %s '<json>' | base64)"`. The JSON is shell-quoted with single quotes (shellQuote: `'` → `'\''`). Extract via regex: match `/printf %s '(.*?)' \| base64/` — but JSON may contain single quotes? JSON.stringify output won't contain `'` characters (they'd be escaped as `\'`... actually JSON strings escape `"` but not `'`; a title containing `'` would break my naive regex). For test fixtures I'll avoid quotes in titles.

Actually wait — there's a subtlety: shellQuote produces `'...'` and any `'` inside becomes `'\''`, so regex `/printf %s '(.*)' \| base64/` with greedy `.*` would capture up to the last `' | base64` — hmm, the payload is the LAST printf in the command, and the command ends with `| base64)"`. Greedy match works if only one occurrence. Fine for fixtures.

Alternatively — simpler and less brittle: parse via index operations. I'll go with the regex.

